== the maps of the two theorems, run on the files (test_pick_windows.py)
Random tasks (test_taskcore's), 300 from seed 1, four configurations (PRODUCT_LIMIT 1 with no lever and with every lever,
PRODUCT_LIMIT 2, the default): Fast Downward's astar(blind()) gives the task's own optimum off and on in every case (252 tasks per
configuration; 250, 214, 240 and 3 of them with a window); 816 optimal plans each way mapped to the other file and run there at the same cost; decode reads the same steps from
both in all 816. 299 files with no window and no pick operator are the same bytes off and on. 0 failures.
The same on 60 tasks from seed 3: 164 plans each way, 54 of them through a window (68 and 65 windows).
On the packed files, Π^W's optimal plan mapped to Π and run there at the same cost, with the same decoded steps: the bar door, the
kitchen, k = 1, the kitchen F1c; Π's lama-first plan (bar door, kitchen) and A* plan (kitchen) mapped to Π^W the same way. None of
these plans uses a consumer. 10 random operator sequences of 30 steps each way on the bar door: mapped, the same facts and cost.
No consumer of the bar door applies in the first 20,000 states of a breadth-first search over Π's other operators.

